+---
+name: deliverables
+description: Build and verify the requested file artifacts (xlsx workbooks, docx reports, csv outputs) for a client deliverable task
+---
+
+# Building and verifying deliverables
+
+## 1. Manifest first
+List every requested artifact with its exact output path, required tabs/sections, columns/fields, and limits (page caps, naming). Confirm each item maps to a line of the task text before building.
+
+## 2. Skeleton every artifact immediately
+Create each file with its full structure (tab names, section headings, column headers) plus any values already computed. A complete-but-rough file on disk beats a perfect one that never gets written; improve in place afterwards.
+
+## 3. Excel mechanics (openpyxl)
+- Write computed values, not formulas: nothing recalculates them, so any `data_only` reader sees None where a number should be.
+- Bold headers and frozen top row on data tabs; explicit number formats for currency, percent, and rate columns.
+- Put the weighting rationale / assumptions block on the tab that uses it, not only in chat.
+- Scratch and intermediate files go to /tmp — or a workspace dotfolder such as `.scratch/` when /tmp is blocked — never into the deliverables folder.
+
+## 4. Word mechanics (python-docx)
+- Use real heading styles for sections; use tables for matrices (go/no-go grids, scoring tables) rather than prose.
+- Respect page limits; estimate length from word count before finalizing.
+
+## 5. Verify before closing
+Run `python3 scripts/verify_artifacts.py <produced files>`: it reopens each file with an independent reader and flags empty sheets, formula-only cells, header-less tabs, and unreadable files. Fix what it flags and re-run. Then walk the manifest item by item against the task text.
